# HOSTS - names PTERM can be given at its startup prompt.
# Address first, like /etc/hosts. Aliases after the first name work.
#
# Tried BEFORE the module's DNS, which does work - the answer is read out of
# host memory with OSWORD 5. This file is the local override, and it is also
# what works with the network down.
#
# Note the module does NOT append a search domain: PTERM asks for the bare
# name and then for name.lan, which is what resolv.conf does on the Linux side.
192.0.2.10 deskbox
192.0.2.20 beeb
192.0.2.30 archbox
